-- ── Decision refinements DISCOVERED during the round ───────────────
-- E8-as-implemented (pre-registered in the pre file, confirmed by a pinned
--   test): the fold-key value component is Some(node_type) for v3
--   (Assertion-ident) records and None for Legacy — the phase spec's literal
--   «(id, node_type, AssertIdent)» would have broken the D8/D9 v2
--   winner-collapse (derived_merge_collapses_v2_records_newest_wins pins a
--   v2 duplicate id with TWO types collapsing) and, with all-Legacy idents
--   at tick 0, flipped the post-compaction winner by TYPE order — a C3
--   violation. §3.2's aid semantics are assertion semantics; v2 records are
--   the record model.
-- E8a (pre-registered): node_candidates' dedup key gained the value column
--   — without it the C3 both-survive gate would be invisible to facts reads.
-- Candidate dedup in the resolver = (node_type, source, generation) — the
--   aid identity (fid ⊃ value); same-aid re-writes newest-wins (M1 = P7).
-- min-fid split side attribution: R8a recorded "20/19" without sides; the
--   re-measurement pins EXTERNAL_FUNCTION = 20, GLOBAL_DEFINITION = 19.
-- Winner-tick Int column: a tick that does not fit i64 is a contractual
--   panic at emission (production ticks are generations ≪ i64; recorded).

